          "params": [],
          "returnType": null,
          "description": "How much of the extracted highlight is added back. 0 leaves the input untouched, 1 adds the full excess over the threshold, higher values push a brighter glow. Default 1."
        },
        {
          "name": "levels",
          "signature": "levels?: number",
          "signatureTokens": [
            {
              "text": "levels",
              "kind": "name"
            },
            {
              "text": "?",
              "kind": "punctuation"
            },
            {
              "text": ": ",
              "kind": "punctuation"
            },
            {
              "text": "number",
              "kind": "keyword"
            }
          ],
          "params": [],
          "returnType": null,
          "description": "Halvings between the input and the level the blur runs on, 1..5. A cost knob rather than a shape knob: the same strength covers the same distance at every setting, and raising it buys that distance at a quarter of the fill rate per level. What it does change is the base of the glow, which gets softer and coarser as the blur runs on fewer texels. A node too small to take every halving takes as many as it can. Default 3."
        },
        {
          "name": "quality",
          "signature": "quality?: number",
          "signatureTokens": [
